{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs24 1.0.3 | 04/24/26\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs20 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab Added two variants to the {\b Fight List} right-click menu for exporting selected fights: {\b Export Selected Fights (with adds)} keeps the existing behavior (writes every combat line in the selected fights' time window, including ambient adds, trash, and wand procs), and {\b Export Selected Fights (without adds)} filters to only the selected fight names — dropping unrelated NPCs that overlapped in time. The "without adds" variant is the right choice for sharing exports across multiple players' logs: each imported file contributes exactly the fights selected, with no phantom fights from overlapping encounters. Single-parse use cases still benefit from the original "with adds" behavior.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs24 1.0.2 | 04/23/26\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs20 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab Fixed duplicate named-pet rows in {\b DPS Summary}. Some non-melee direct-damage lines (e.g. {\b Blood Fountain} procs from Bonaparte) were still leaving a trailing space on the attacker name, so the same pet appeared as two rows in the DPS breakdown. The pet now correctly rolls up as a single row under the owning player.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs20 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab Fixed a phantom DPS row that showed only a time value and no damage. Pet miss lines such as {\b "Bonaparte  tries to bash NPC, but NPC is INVULNERABLE!"} were registering a separate attacker entry because of the trailing space on the pet name, producing an empty row alongside the real one.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs20 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 3.\tx360\tab Fixed {\b pet owner mis-attribution} in raid logs. The parser was assigning every named pet it saw (including other players' pets like {\b Fireballs} or {\b Otto}) to the character whose log was being parsed, overwriting correct mappings in {\b petmapping.txt}. Pets are now marked as pets but ownership is only set from {\b petmapping.txt}, the pet's own {\b "My leader is X"} announcement, or the {\b Pet Owners} window.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs24 1.0.1 | 04/21/26\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs20 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab Fixed pet DPS attribution. Named pet attacker names are now trimmed of their trailing space at the point of detection so damage records store the clean name. Previously the trailing space caused pet DPS lookups to miss, keeping named pets as separate rows in DPS Summary instead of rolling up under their owner.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs20 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab Added support for {\b Dalaya's damage shield} lines ({\b "X was hit by non-melee for Y points of damage"}). The parser now defers attribution until the immediately following melee hit identifies the shielded player. DS damage is now correctly credited to the player wearing the shield rather than being dropped.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs20 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 3.\tx360\tab Fixed duplicate pet entries in the {\b Pet Owners} window. Pet names are now trimmed at the point of entry in {\b AddPetToPlayer} and {\b AddVerifiedPet}, with a safety-net trim in {\b GetPlayerFromPet} and {\b IsVerifiedPet} as well.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs24 1.0.0 | 04/21/26\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs20 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab Initial release of {\b EQLogParser-Dalaya}, a fork of {\b EQLogParser} by kauffman12 (v2.3.50), customized for the {\b Dalaya} EverQuest emulation server.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs20 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab Rewrote {\b damage line parsing} to support Dalaya's log format. Dalaya uses {\b "X has taken N damage from your SpellName"} for player spells and {\b "X has taken N damage from AttackerName by SpellName"} for group/pet spells, which is the reverse of the live EQ format.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs20 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 3.\tx360\tab Added correct attribution of {\b player DoT and DD spell damage} to the casting player. Previously all spell damage was misattributed to a phantom entity or shown as separate DPS rows.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs20 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 4.\tx360\tab Added support for {\b named pets} (e.g. Bonaparte, Fireballs, Otto). Dalaya logs named pets with a double-space after their name, which is now detected and used to reliably identify them as pets and link them to their owner.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs20 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 5.\tx360\tab Fixed {\b pet spell damage} attribution. Spells cast by named pets such as Blood Fountain and Caustic Mist are now correctly shown under the pet owner's DPS rather than as a separate player.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs20 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 6.\tx360\tab Fixed {\b other players' spell damage} attribution. Spells cast by group and raid members (e.g. {\b "from Puckin by Ancient: Fatebind"}) are now correctly identified and attributed to the casting player.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs20 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 7.\tx360\tab Replaced the {\b spells.txt} database with one generated from Dalaya's {\b spells_us.txt}. This ensures spell names, landing messages, and spell classifications reflect Dalaya's custom spells rather than live EQ spells which share IDs but have different names and effects.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs20 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 8.\tx360\tab Fixed the {\b Damaging} field in the spells database so that {\b GetDamagingSpellByName} correctly identifies Dalaya spells, enabling accurate DoT vs DD classification.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs20 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 9.\tx360\tab Fixed {\b pet ownership persistence}. The {\b PlayerManager.Save()} method previously excluded named pets with trailing spaces from being written to {\b petmapping.txt} due to a name validation check. Pet-to-owner mappings now survive application restarts.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs20 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 10.\tx360\tab Disabled {\b EMU Parsing mode} requirement for Dalaya. Dalaya uses a newer log format that does not require the legacy EMU parsing toggle, which was causing spell and damage lines to be swapped incorrectly when enabled.\sa180\par}
}